# On top of M8's config: the DECON/DSI display stack in place of simpledrm,
# the Tensor TMU so the big-core thermal zone can throttle, and a ramoops
# console so a failed boot leaves a log in /sys/fs/pstore. nf_tables for
# Nura's default nftables firewall, and zram (zstd) for postmarketos-zram-swap.
# Waydroid: Android's netd needs policy routing (ip rule / per-network
# tables; without it no default route is ever installed) and the xt
# matches/targets plus cls_bpf from Android's base kernel config.
# Lockup detectors that panic, plus an auto reboot, so silent freezes leave a
# trace in ramoops (a forced power-off wipes it).
# Scheduling like Android's gs101 kernel: uclamp (schedutil otherwise runs
# every RT task, e.g. PipeWire's data loop and the panfrost/ufs IRQ threads,
# at the cluster's max frequency; with uclamp the device package drops the RT
# default boost and userspace can boost the UI instead), the TEO cpuidle
# governor and the multi-gen LRU.
# Cameras: M8's tree has the gs101 MIPI-CSIS receiver (raw Bayer through the
# CSIS write-DMA, no ISP), its D/C-PHY, the IMX355 (front), S5KGN1 (rear) and
# IMX386 (ultrawide) sensors, their SLG51000 PMIC, the LM3644 flash/torch and
# the VL53L1X laser ranger; the DT nodes are already enabled. The SLG51000 is
# switched on through S2MPG11 GPIOs, so it needs GPIO_S2MPG1X too. libcamera's
# simple pipeline + SoftISP does the rest.
# Game controllers (USB and Bluetooth): hidraw (Steam Input and SDL talk to
# pads through it), joydev, xpad and the HID drivers for DualShock/DualSense,
# Steam, Switch, Xbox (Bluetooth), Logitech and Stadia pads, with rumble.
